Subject: [PATCH] BRINGUP: iommu/qcom: Tolerate the rateless Venus codec clock

The MMCC driver registers venus0_vcodec0_clk but not its parent
vcodec0_clk_src, so clk_round_rate() returns zero. The first multimedia
power probe aborted with -EINVAL at clock 121 before reaching the
probe-only stop: the five domains and the other 14 clocks had been set
up, cleanup returned, and SSH and the watchdog stayed healthy.

Enable that known gate without a rate, and keep aborting the probe on
any other clock that cannot produce one, so the remaining multimedia
SMMUs can be exercised. The real fix is to register the missing clock
source in mmcc-msm8994.

Apply with git apply after 0033; uncommitted bring-up diff.

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -824,10 +824,26 @@
 		}
 		if (!clk_get_rate(clk)) {
 			rate = clk_round_rate(clk, 1);
-			ret = rate <= 0 ? -EINVAL : clk_set_rate(clk, rate);
-			if (ret) {
-				clk_put(clk);
-				goto out;
+			if (rate <= 0) {
+				/*
+				 * The MMCC driver never registers vcodec0_clk_src,
+				 * the parent of VENUS0_VCODEC0_CLK. Enable that
+				 * gate without a rate; any other clock that cannot
+				 * produce one still aborts the probe.
+				 */
+				if (clock_ids[i] != VENUS0_VCODEC0_CLK) {
+					ret = rate < 0 ? (int)rate : -EINVAL;
+					clk_put(clk);
+					goto out;
+				}
+				dev_warn(dev, "iommu sec: MM clock %u has no rate source, enabling gate only\n",
+					 clock_ids[i]);
+			} else {
+				ret = clk_set_rate(clk, rate);
+				if (ret) {
+					clk_put(clk);
+					goto out;
+				}
 			}
 		}
 		ret = clk_prepare_enable(clk);
